dx - Run Bazel workflows

dx <command> [flags] [scope ...] [-- bazel-options ...]

Scopes: labels, patterns, files, or dirs. No scope means //... for commands that take scopes.

Exit codes: 0 success, 2 usage error, 1 failed check.

Usage: dx [COMMAND]

Commands:
  security    run security audit over resolved scopes (non-mutating; live Gitleaks plus advisory/vuln backends)
  license     run license audit over resolved scopes (non-mutating)
  lint        run lint analysis over resolved scopes (check by default; --apply writes fixes)
  typecheck   run typecheck analysis over resolved scopes (check by default; --apply writes fixes)
  format      check or rewrite formatting over resolved scopes (check by default; --apply writes fixes)
  generate    update BUILD declarations from source with Gazelle (check by default; --apply writes)
  build       run Bazel build over resolved targets
  test        run Bazel test over resolved targets
  coverage    collect LCOV coverage with optional threshold
  bench       run dx-bench tagged tests and print their numbers
  run         build and run runnable targets sequentially (explicit labels/patterns; file/dir scopes need exactly one runnable)
  deploy      build and run a single deployable target
  check       run generate+format+lint+typecheck in order (check by default; --apply writes fixes, then verifies with a read-only check)
  clean       prune unselected managed state, never Bazel outputs; use `bazel clean` for those (check by default; --apply prunes; no scopes)
  update      update dependencies per set, or widen or add one package to a version (check by default; --apply writes)
  env         collect managed tools and generated source (check by default; --apply writes managed state)
  init        start or adopt a dx workspace in this or a new directory (check by default; --apply scaffolds and is safe to re-run)
  upgrade     move the pin to any version, newer or older, and refresh existing launchers and the AGENTS.md block (check by default; --apply moves)
  status      report workspace status; --capabilities adds command capabilities
  watch       watch for changes and rebuild (local only)
  completion  emit shell completions from the CLI grammar (bash|zsh|fish|powershell)
  docs        build and serve the mdBook documentation site, or an API index of the Rust libraries in scope (non-mutating)
  worktree    lease warm checkout slots (add, release, list, path, prune; prune checks by default, --apply deletes)
  explain     explain why actions missed the cache by diffing two execution logs from build/test --explain (non-mutating)
  fuzz        run dx-fuzz targets for a time budget and store crashes under .dx/fuzz

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Environment:
  DX_WORKSPACE=<dir>
      Default for --workspace.
  DX_QUIET=<bool>
      Default for --quiet.
  DX_VERBOSE=<bool>
      Default for --verbose.
  DX_COLOR=<mode>
      Default for --color.
  DX_OUTPUT=<mode>
      Default for --output.
  DX_FAIL_ON=<level>
      Default for --fail-on.
  DX_BUILD_SLOTS=<auto|n|off>
      Default for --build-slots.
  <bool> is on for true and off for false.
      Anything else is a usage error. An empty value is unset.
  <auto|n|off> sizes build slots from memory, takes exactly n (1-1024), or takes none.
  NO_COLOR=<non-empty>
      Disable color output.
  BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY=<dir>
      Workspace start under `bazel run`.
  BUILD_WORKING_DIRECTORY=<dir>
      Current directory under `bazel run`, for `--here` and a relative `worktree release <path>`.
  In CI the DX_ variables are ignored; flags still win.
